<title>USA: Clinton asked to back securities suits standards.</title>
<headline>Clinton asked to back securities suits standards.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton was asked by 57 House Democrats Thursday to back legislation establishing uniform national standards for private securities class action suits.</p>
<p>Rep. Anna Eshoo of California said the national standards were needed because of a sharp increase in securities suits filed in state courts since passage of a federal law two years ago restricting such suits.</p>
<p>&quot;Companies are forced to deal with 50 different laws, none of which provide the protections contained in the federal statute,&quot; Eshoo said in a statement.</p>
</text>
